-- Abutment — acoustic illusion / jazz-adjacent (companion to Cantilever)
-- Reassuring acoustic music: after the failure, the surviving abutment becomes
-- the survey datum, takes the temporary props, is enlarged, and finally carries
-- the load. 90 BPM home · D major. Lazy swing, through-composed, seven sections
-- in four acts, with an open coda.
--
-- Only Dirt-Samples acoustic banks are used — double bass, brushed kit, ride,
-- plucked piano, sax, trumpet sparkles, woodblock, glass taps, metal, breath
-- and wind. No custom samples, no pads/arps/casio-style timbres.
--
-- Eval the setup block below once (one `let` block), then play the sections in
-- order: All Clear → Survey → Shore → Abutment → Transfer → Occupancy → Steady.
--
-- Gotchas: reverb size <= 0.9; `amp` is linear (prefer it to `gain`).
--
-- Story — Cantilever ends with the snap; Abutment starts after the dust settles.
-- The projecting span is gone; the heavy block at the anchored end survived. It
-- was never the visible idea, but it did not fail. The piece is not about
-- building a bigger cantilever — it is about returning the load to the thing
-- that can carry it:
--   1. All Clear — the site is declared safe; the abutment stands alone, exposed.
--   2. Survey — the wreck is measured from the one thing that has not moved;
--      the abutment becomes the datum.
--   3. Shore — temporary props take the broken stub and cables run the load back
--      into the abutment; the first weight since the failure.
--   4. Abutment — the old block is underpinned and new mass is keyed in behind
--      it; tempo lifts, sax enters, warm maj9/6-9 chords.
--   5. Transfer — the props are eased out and the load moves into the abutment;
--      a sus4 hangs, then resolves. It holds.
--   6. Occupancy — the span is rebuilt and reopened; people return, warm melody,
--      plagal G–D cadence, brighter but grateful, not triumphant.
--   7. Steady — evening; the structure rests and the load is carried silently.
-- The reassurance is that the conflict is already over. The last thing we hear
-- is the support, not the span.
--
-- Stream map (dN is a stream slot; Tidal sends it to SuperDirt orbit N-1):
--   d1  soft kick / foot      kickSoft / kickSparse
--   d2  brushes               brushSoft / brush / brushWork
--   d3  ride                  rideSoft / ride / rideBell
--   d4  piano low / comping   pianoPedal / compSurvey … compOcc / pianoSteady
--   d5  piano high / colour   pianoColour / colourSurvey … colourOcc / pianoAfter
--   d6  double bass           bassPedal / bassSurvey / bassShore / bassAbut /
--                             bassTrans / bassOcc / bassSteady
--   d7  sax                   reedShore / reedAbut / reedTrans / reedOcc
--   d8  trumpet sparkle       trumpetOcc / trumpetSteady
--   d9  tools / site sounds   woodTick / plumb / knock / metalTool / wood
--   d10 air / room            air / windBed / gravel
--
-- Structure (~11½ min, open coda):
--   Act I. Assess
--     1. All Clear — the abutment alone; dust settles (90 BPM, 28 cycles, ~1:15).
--     2. Survey — the datum; measured from the survivor (90 BPM, 36 cycles, ~1:36).
--   Act II. Repair
--     3. Shore — props and tie-backs take the stub (90 BPM, 36 cycles, ~1:36).
--     4. Abutment — underpinned; new mass keyed in (94 BPM, 40 cycles, ~1:42).
--   Act III. Return
--     5. Transfer — props eased out; the load moves in (92 BPM, 36 cycles, ~1:34).
--     6. Occupancy — rebuilt, reopened, people return (90 BPM, 40 cycles, ~1:47).
--   Act IV. Rest
--     7. Steady — evening; the load is held; open coda (86 BPM, 40+ cycles, ~1:52+).
--
-- How to run:
--   1. Start SuperDirt/audio with scripts/up.sh and open Tidal in Emacs.
--   2. Eval the setup block below as one block.
--   3. Work through sections 1→7. Each section glides to its tempo over 16 s
--      (glideBpm in boot/BootTidal.hs), rather than jumping. If glideBpm is not
--      in scope, restart the Tidal REPL (C-c C-s) so the boot reloads.
--   4. Section 7 (Steady) is open-ended. Leave the last chord and air ringing,
--      then evaluate fadeSilence 24 [4,5,6,8,10]; only after the room has
--      decayed, evaluate hush on its own.
--
-- Notes:
--   - Relationship to Cantilever — Cantilever is D dorian and ends in the snap.
--     Abutment answers in D major: the same ensemble, the same room, but the low
--     register carries the argument and the cadences are plagal (G–D). The
--     unresolved sus chords stand for the load; the six-nine and maj-nine
--     chords are the reassurance.
--   - Four acts — Assess (1–2), Repair (3–4), Return (5–6) and Rest (7).
--     Abutment is the turn; Transfer is the resolution; Occupancy is the return
--     to normal; Steady is the open coda.
--   - Shared helpers — speedAt, swing8, swing16, chordAt and fadeSilence are
--     defined in boot/BootTidal.hs; the setup only defines this track's voices.
--   - Swing — swing8 = swingBy (1/5) 4 (8th-note lilt) and swing16 = swingBy
--     (1/5) 8 (16th-note lilt). The offbeats lean back.
--   - Tuning — pitched samples are calibrated with speedAt base p: bass1:0 = C2
--     (c3), pluck:5 = C3 (c4), pluck:8 = D4 (d5), sax:5 = C3 (c4), trump:5 = B5
--     (b6), trump:7 = E6 (e7). Written pitches are Tidal letter names, one octave
--     above scientific pitch.
--   - One-shots — each voice triggers its sample once; sustain and release
--     shape the tail.
--   - Chords — harmony is built with Sound.Tidal.Chords (chordAt), not
--     hand-written voicings. The boot file exposes tidal-core so the chord
--     module is importable.
--   - Levels — this track uses amp (linear) rather than gain (amp * gain^4);
--     reverb size <= 0.9. The mix has not been balanced by ear yet, so expect to
--     trim amp values once you hear it. The trumpet is deliberately quiet and
--     distant.
--   - Tempo glides — setbpm jumps the clock, so section boundaries use
--     glideBpm target 16 (boot/BootTidal.hs). It forks and steps the tempo 10×/s,
--     so the sender is not blocked; each glide starts from the tempo current at
--     call time. Overlapping glides are not cancelled, so leave a section
--     playing long enough for its 16 s glide to finish.
--   - Trumpet — trumpetOcc and trumpetSteady use slow 16, so each written note
--     lands once every 16 cycles. Expect long silences between stabs.
--   - Open coda — section 7 (Steady) does not stop itself. fadeSilence and hush
--     are separate blocks; evaluate them in order, with a pause between.

setbpm 90

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Voices / patterns. One `let` block: eval all at once (C-RET).
-- Harmony: D major, voiced with Sound.Tidal.Chords.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
let
  -- Shared helpers (speedAt, swing8, swing16, chordAt, fadeSilence)
  -- live in boot/BootTidal.hs. Only track-specific voices belong here.
  -- --- harmony: D major, through-composed --------------------------------
  -- Warm, plagal-leaning. The unresolved sus chords are the load; the
  -- six-nine and maj-nine chords are the reassurance.
  hClear = chordAt "<d4 a4 g4 d4>" "<sus2 add9 sixNine maj9>"
  hSurvey = chordAt "<d4 g4 d4 a4>" "<maj9 sixNine add9 sevenSus4>"
  hShore = chordAt "<b3 g4 d4 a4>" "<min9 sixNine maj9 sevenSus4>"
  hAbut = chordAt "<g4 d4 a4 b3>" "<sixNine maj9 sevenSus4 min9>"
  hTrans = chordAt "<d4 d4 g4 a4 d4>" "<sus4 major sixNine sevenSus4 sixNine>"
  hOcc = chordAt "<g4 d4 a4 d4>" "<sixNine maj9 add9 sixNine>"
  hSteady = chordAt "<d4 b3 g4 d4>" "<maj9 min9 sixNine sixNine>"
  -- --- piano: pluck samples tuned to their natural pitches -----------------
  -- pluck:5 is C3, pluck:8 is D4 (scientific pitch; Tidal c4/d5).
  -- Each voice plays its sample once; `sustain` decides how long it rings.
  pianoPedal = s "pluck" # n 5 # speedAt "c4" (chordAt "d4" "sus2")
    # sustain 2.2 # release 1 # lpf 1700 # lpq 0.25
    # room 0.62 # size 0.78 # amp 0.62
  pianoComp p = s "pluck" # n 5 # speedAt "c4" p
    # sustain 0.6 # release 0.25 # lpf 2800 # lpq 0.3
    # room 0.4 # size 0.55 # amp 0.78
  pianoSteady = s "pluck" # n 5 # speedAt "c4" (slow 4 hSteady)
    # sustain 2 # release 1.2 # lpf 1500 # lpq 0.25
    # room 0.68 # size 0.82 # amp 0.6
  pianoColour p = s "pluck" # n 8 # speedAt "d5" p
    # sustain 0.8 # release 0.3 # lpf 4200
    # room 0.52 # size 0.66 # amp 0.66
  pianoAfter = s "pluck" # n 8 # speedAt "d5" ((slow 4 hSteady) |+ 12)
    # sustain 2 # release 1.2 # lpf 2000 # lpq 0.25
    # room 0.72 # size 0.84 # amp 0.5
  -- --- comping: chords on a rhythm, then swung -----------------------------
  compSurvey = swing8 (struct "t ~ ~ t ~ ~ t ~" (pianoComp (slow 3 hSurvey)))
  compShore = swing8 (struct "t ~ ~ t ~ ~ t ~" (pianoComp (slow 3 hShore)))
  compAbut = swing8 (struct "t t ~ ~ t ~ ~ t" (pianoComp (slow 2 hAbut)))
  compTrans = swing8 (struct "t ~ t ~ ~ t ~ ~" (pianoComp (slow 2 hTrans)))
  compOcc = swing8 (struct "t ~ t ~ ~ t ~ ~" (pianoComp (slow 2 hOcc)))
  colourSurvey = swing16 (struct "~ ~ t ~ ~ ~ ~ t" (pianoColour ((slow 3 hSurvey) |+ 12)))
  colourShore = swing16 (struct "~ ~ t ~ ~ t ~ ~" (pianoColour ((slow 3 hShore) |+ 12)))
  colourAbut = swing16 (struct "~ t ~ ~ t ~ ~ t" (pianoColour ((slow 2 hAbut) |+ 12)))
  colourTrans = swing16 (struct "~ ~ t ~ ~ ~ t ~" (pianoColour ((slow 2 hTrans) |+ 12)))
  colourOcc = swing16 (struct "~ ~ t ~ ~ t ~ ~" (pianoColour ((slow 2 hOcc) |+ 12)))
  -- --- double bass: bass1:0 is C2 (Tidal c3) ------------------------------
  -- The bass is the abutment: it stays low and gains weight through the middle.
  bassPedal = slow 2 $ s "bass1" # n 2 # speedAt "c3" "d3 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~"
    # sustain 2.8 # release 1.2 # lpf 480 # lpq 0.18
    # room 0.5 # size 0.65 # amp 0.82
  bassSurvey = swing8 $ s "bass1" # n "<2 2 12 10>" # speedAt "c3" "d3 ~ fs3 a3 ~ cs4 ~ a2"
    # sustain 0.7 # release 0.25 # lpf 780 # lpq 0.24
    # room 0.26 # size 0.4 # amp 0.88
  bassShore = swing8 $ s "bass1" # n "<2 12 2 10>" # speedAt "c3" "b2 ~ d3 fs3 ~ a3 ~ g2"
    # sustain 0.8 # release 0.28 # lpf 720 # lpq 0.22
    # room 0.28 # size 0.44 # amp 0.88
  bassAbut = swing8 $ s "bass1" # n "<2 12 2 10>" # speedAt "c3" "g2 ~ d3 ~ a2 ~ b2 ~"
    # sustain 0.6 # release 0.22 # lpf 900 # lpq 0.26
    # room 0.24 # size 0.4 # amp 0.9
  bassTrans = swing8 $ s "bass1" # n 2 # speedAt "c3" "d3 ~ ~ ~ a2 ~ ~ ~"
    # sustain 1.4 # release 0.5 # lpf 620 # lpq 0.2
    # room 0.35 # size 0.52 # amp 0.86
  bassOcc = swing8 $ s "bass1" # n "<2 12 2 12>" # speedAt "c3" "g2 ~ d3 ~ a2 ~ d3 ~"
    # sustain 0.8 # release 0.3 # lpf 760 # lpq 0.22
    # room 0.3 # size 0.46 # amp 0.88
  bassSteady = slow 2 $ s "bass1" # n 2 # speedAt "c3" "d3 ~ ~ ~ a2 ~ ~ ~"
    # sustain 2 # release 1 # lpf 520 # lpq 0.18
    # room 0.55 # size 0.72 # amp 0.78
  -- --- brushes / ride: gretsch acoustic kit -------------------------------
  kickSoft = s "~ gretsch ~ gretsch" # n 13 # sustain 0.45 # release 0.15
    # lpf 340 # room 0.16 # size 0.28 # amp 0.7
  kickSparse = slow 2 $ s "gretsch" # n 13 # sustain 0.45 # release 0.18
    # lpf 320 # room 0.18 # size 0.3 # amp 0.72
  brushSoft = s "~ ~ gretsch ~" # n 3 # sustain 0.3 # release 0.15
    # lpf 2600 # room 0.35 # size 0.5 # amp 0.42
  brush = swing8 $ s "~ gretsch ~ gretsch" # n "<3 2>" # sustain 0.3 # release 0.16
    # lpf 3000 # room 0.28 # size 0.42 # amp 0.58
  brushWork = swing8 $ s "gretsch ~ gretsch ~" # n 3 # sustain 0.28 # release 0.14
    # lpf 3200 # room 0.3 # size 0.44 # amp 0.6
  rideSoft = swing8 $ s "gretsch:19 ~ gretsch:19 ~ gretsch:19 ~ gretsch:19 ~"
    # sustain 0.3 # release 0.15 # lpf 5000 # room 0.26 # size 0.4 # amp 0.4
  ride = swing8 $ s "gretsch:19 ~ gretsch:19 gretsch:19 ~ gretsch:19 ~ gretsch:19"
    # sustain 0.35 # release 0.15 # lpf 5600 # room 0.24 # size 0.38 # amp 0.55
  rideBell = swing8 $ s "~ ~ ~ gretsch:18 ~ ~ ~ ~" # sustain 0.3 # release 0.2
    # lpf 6400 # room 0.3 # size 0.48 # amp 0.42
  -- --- tools / site sounds ------------------------------------------------
  woodTick = swing8 $ s "~ ~ east ~ ~ ~ east ~" # n 0
    # room 0.3 # size 0.38 # amp 0.38
  plumb = degradeBy 0.35 $ slow 2 $ s "~ ~ glasstap ~" # n (irand 3)
    # speed (range 0.9 1.3 $ slow 8 rand) # hpf 800 # lpf 6000
    # room 0.45 # size 0.55 # amp 0.32
  knock = degradeBy 0.3 $ slow 2 $ s "~ east ~ ~" # n 1
    # room 0.4 # size 0.5 # amp 0.4
  metalTool = degradeBy 0.5 $ slow 4 $ s "metal" # n (irand 10) # sustain 0.6
    # speed (range 0.5 0.9 $ slow 4 rand) # hpf 260 # lpf 2400 # pan rand
    # room 0.58 # size 0.76 # amp 0.28
  wood = swing8 $ s "~ ~ east ~ ~ ~ east ~" # n 0
    # room 0.3 # size 0.38 # amp 0.34
  -- --- air / room ---------------------------------------------------------
  air = slow 8 $ s "breath" # n 0 # sustain 0.5 # hpf 500 # lpf 2400
    # room 0.65 # size 0.82 # amp 0.34
  windBed = slow 4 $ s "wind" # n (irand 10) # sustain 8
    # hpf 400 # lpf 1500 # room 0.7 # size 0.85 # amp 0.22
  gravel = degradeBy 0.6 $ slow 8 $ s "pebbles"
    # speed (range 0.6 1.1 $ slow 8 rand) # hpf 500 # lpf 3000
    # room 0.7 # size 0.85 # amp 0.12
  -- --- sax: sax:5 is C3 (Tidal c4) ----------------------------------------
  reedShore = slow 4 $ s "sax" # n 5 # speedAt "c4" "d4 ~ ~ ~ a4 ~ ~ ~"
    # sustain 2 # release 0.9 # hpf 150 # lpf 1200 # lpq 0.2
    # room 0.62 # size 0.8 # amp 0.32
  reedAbut = slow 2 $ s "sax" # n 5 # speedAt "c4" "d4 ~ fs4 ~ a4 ~ g4 ~"
    # sustain 1.4 # release 0.6 # hpf 150 # lpf 1500 # lpq 0.25
    # room 0.6 # size 0.78 # amp 0.4
  reedTrans = slow 8 $ s "sax" # n 5 # speedAt "c4" "a4 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~"
    # sustain 5 # release 2.2 # hpf 140 # lpf 1100 # lpq 0.2
    # room 0.72 # size 0.85 # amp 0.34
  reedOcc = slow 2 $ s "sax" # n 5 # speedAt "c4" "g4 ~ a4 ~ d5 ~ b4 ~"
    # sustain 1.2 # release 0.55 # hpf 160 # lpf 1700 # lpq 0.25
    # room 0.58 # size 0.76 # amp 0.42
  -- --- trumpet: high, distant, never featured -----------------------------
  -- trump:5 is B5 (Tidal b6); trump:7 is E6 (Tidal e7).
  trumpetOcc = slow 16 $ s "trump" # n 5 # speedAt "b6" "~ ~ ~ ~ d6 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~"
    # sustain 0.5 # release 0.35 # lpf 3000 # lpq 0.2 # room 0.7 # size 0.8 # amp 0.22
  trumpetSteady = slow 16 $ s "trump" # n 7 # speedAt "e7" "~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ a6 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~"
    # sustain 0.5 # release 0.4 # hpf 300 # lpf 1600 # lpq 0.25 # room 0.8 # size 0.85 # amp 0.16

-- 1. All Clear — the failure is over. The abutment stands alone; dust settles.
-- ~28 cycles (~75 s at 90 BPM).

glideBpm 90 16
-- clear the previous piece's working streams
fadeSilence 8 [1,2,3,7,8,9]

-- the surviving mass: a low D pedal and a sus2 piano
d4 pianoPedal
d6 $ bassPedal # amp 0.2
-- the room breathes
d10 air
-- one high shadow, far away
xfadeIn 5 24 $ pianoColour (slow 4 hClear |+ 12) # amp 0.4 # lpf 2600

-- 2. Survey — the wreck is measured from the abutment; it becomes the datum.
-- ~36 cycles (~96 s at 90 BPM).

glideBpm 90 16
-- the datum holds: bass and low piano
d6 $ bassSurvey # amp 0.3
xfadeIn 4 16 compSurvey

-- plumb-line ticks and a cautious swing
fadeMulti 12 [
  (9, stack [plumb, woodTick]),
  (2, brushSoft),
  (3, rideSoft),
  -- first colour above
  (5, pianoColour (slow 3 hSurvey |+ 12) # amp 0.45 # lpf 3200)]

-- 3. Shore — props take the broken stub; cables run back to the abutment.
-- ~36 cycles (~96 s at 90 BPM).

glideBpm 90 16
-- the load returns to the abutment
d6 $ bassShore # amp 0.3
xfadeIn 4 16 compShore

-- work rhythm
fadeMulti 16 [
  (1, kickSoft),
  (2, brushWork),
  (3, ride),
  (9, stack [woodTick, knock])]
-- a distant reed hears the work
xfadeIn 7 32 reedShore

-- 4. Abutment — the old block is underpinned; new mass is keyed in behind it.
-- ~40 cycles (~102 s at 94 BPM).

glideBpm 94 16
d2 brush
d3 $ stack [ride, rideBell]
xfadeIn 5 24 colourAbut
-- light swing
d6 $ bassAbut # amp 0.5
xfadeIn 4 16 compAbut

-- the reed enters properly
xfadeIn 7 24 reedAbut

-- the reed doesn't seem to stop
xfadeIn 7 24 silence

-- the new mass: wood, metal and site air
xfadeIn 9 16 $ degradeBy 0.4 (stack [woodTick, metalTool])
xfadeIn 10 32 $ stack [air, gravel]

-- 5. Transfer — props eased out; the load moves into the abutment. It holds.
-- ~36 cycles (~94 s at 92 BPM).

glideBpm 92 16
d1 kickSparse
d2 brush
d3 ride
d6 $ bassTrans # amp 0.5
xfadeIn 4 16 compTrans
xfadeIn 5 24 colourTrans

-- the reed holds one long note
d7 reedTrans

-- tools withdraw
fadeSilence 8 [9]

-- air returns
xfadeIn 10 24 $ stack [air, windBed]

-- 6. Occupancy — the span is rebuilt; people return; the abutment disappears
-- under the approach. ~40 cycles (~107 s at 90 BPM).

glideBpm 90 16
d1 kickSoft
d2 brush
d3 (stack [ride, rideBell])
d6 bassOcc
xfadeIn 4 16 compOcc
xfadeIn 5 24 colourOcc

-- the warm melody
d7 reedOcc
fadeMulti 24 [
  (8, trumpetOcc),
  (9, degradeBy 0.5 wood),
  (10, stack [air, gravel]),
  (7, silence)]

-- 7. Steady — evening; the structure rests; the load is held. Open coda.
-- ~40+ cycles (~112 s+ at 86 BPM; open-ended).

glideBpm 86 16
-- strip the rhythm and the high projection
fadeSilence 16 [1,2,3,7,8,9]

-- the abutment remains: low piano, bass and air

d6 $ bassSteady # amp 0.4 -- slowing down

d4 pianoSteady
xfadeIn 10 24 $ stack [air, windBed, gravel]

-- a last high shadow
fadeMulti 24 [
  (5, pianoAfter # amp 0.3),
  (8, trumpetSteady)]
                 
-- leave this ringing, then evaluate the two steps below separately:
-- first fade everything still sounding (24 cycles), and only after the room
-- has decayed, evaluate `hush` on its own.
fadeSilence 24 [4,5,6,8,10]

hush
